  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COMESA Cross-Border Trade Initiative: facilitating small-scale trade across the borders</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;This four years proposed programme aims at increasing the formalisation of informal cross-border trade and enhancing small-scale cross-border trade flows in the Common Market for Eastern and Southern Africa (COMESA)/tripartite region, leading to increased fiscal revenues for governments as well as to increased security and higher incomes for small-scale cross-border traders. This programmes in line with the 11th EDF Regional indicative Programme (RIP) for Eastern Africa, Southern Africa and the Indian Ocean (EA-SA-IO) region, the COMESA Treaty, the 2016-2020 COMESA Medium-Term Strategic Plan and relevant COMESA trade facilitation policies and instruments. It builds also on existing initiatives at national level in the region to promote and facilitate small-scale cross-border trade flows.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
